==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|potens||powerful, strong, potent|lang=la}}, present participle of {{term|posse||to be able}}, from {{term|potis||able, powerful, originally a lord, master}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpəʊtənt/}}
* {{rhymes|əʊtənt}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Possessing [[strength]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''potent''' argument}}
# Being [[effective]] in small [[quantity|quantities]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''potent''' medicine}}
# Having a [[sharp]] or [[offensive]] taste.
# {{context|of a male|lang=en}} Able to [[procreate]].
# [[very|Very]] [[powerful]] or [[effective]].
#* Shakespeare
#*: harsh and '''potent''' injuries
#* Milton
#*: Moses once more his '''potent''' rod extends.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|tincture|lang=en}} A [[heraldic]] [[fur]] formed by a regular [[tessellation]] of blue and white T shapes.
# {{cx|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[prince]]; a [[potentate]].
#: {{rfquotek|Shakespeare}}
# {{cx|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[staff]] or [[crutch]].

